1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,913
You have learned nine things about Jenkins. But can you prove it?

2
00:00:04,463 --> 00:00:06,642
A tutorial that works on the video,

3
00:00:06,642 --> 00:00:09,505
is not the same as a skill that works for you.

4
00:00:09,505 --> 00:00:10,377
In a real job,

5
00:00:10,377 --> 00:00:12,307
someone will ask: does it work?

6
00:00:12,307 --> 00:00:12,805
Show me.

7
00:00:13,355 --> 00:00:14,741
So today is different.

8
00:00:14,741 --> 00:00:16,946
We build one real release pipeline,

9
00:00:16,946 --> 00:00:17,765
from nothing.

10
00:00:17,765 --> 00:00:19,214
And a script checks it,

11
00:00:19,214 --> 00:00:20,915
with seven tests that pass,

12
00:00:20,915 --> 00:00:21,419
or fail.

13
00:00:21,969 --> 00:00:22,838
Seven of seven,

14
00:00:22,838 --> 00:00:24,577
and you have mastered Jenkins.

15
00:00:24,577 --> 00:00:26,374
Then we write down the results,

16
00:00:26,374 --> 00:00:27,302
and we clean up.

17
00:00:28,852 --> 00:00:30,281
Here is what to expect.

18
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:33,541
One: the whole Jenkins domain, on one page.

19
00:00:34,091 --> 00:00:36,373
Two: the scenario, and the seven checks.

20
00:00:36,923 --> 00:00:38,128
Three: a live demo,

21
00:00:38,128 --> 00:00:39,904
in the real Jenkins screens,

22
00:00:39,904 --> 00:00:41,362
and in a real terminal.

23
00:00:41,362 --> 00:00:42,123
We build it,

24
00:00:42,123 --> 00:00:42,884
we check it,

25
00:00:42,884 --> 00:00:43,772
we back it up,

26
00:00:43,772 --> 00:00:45,167
we record the results,

27
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,182
and we clean up.

28
00:00:46,732 --> 00:00:50,017
Four: what to do when a check fails, and where to find the lab.

29
00:00:50,567 --> 00:00:53,597
This is the mastery lesson of the Jenkins domain.

30
00:00:55,147 --> 00:00:59,456
The Jenkins domain, on one page. Nine objectives, nine lessons.

31
00:01:00,006 --> 00:01:01,634
One: the architecture.

32
00:01:01,634 --> 00:01:02,449
Controller,

33
00:01:02,449 --> 00:01:02,967
agents,

34
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:03,707
executors,

35
00:01:03,707 --> 00:01:04,595
and plugins.

36
00:01:04,595 --> 00:01:06,149
Two: install Jenkins,

37
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:08,369
and set up the administration.

38
00:01:08,919 --> 00:01:10,651
Three: the Jenkinsfile,

39
00:01:10,651 --> 00:01:12,238
with stages and steps.

40
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:14,547
Four: build and test CloudCart,

41
00:01:14,547 --> 00:01:15,340
with Maven.

42
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:17,169
Five: credentials,

43
00:01:17,169 --> 00:01:19,016
and environment variables.

44
00:01:19,016 --> 00:01:20,010
Six: triggers,

45
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:21,431
the SonarQube gate,

46
00:01:21,431 --> 00:01:22,141
and Nexus.

47
00:01:22,691 --> 00:01:23,759
Seven: agents,

48
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:24,827
and artifacts.

49
00:01:24,827 --> 00:01:26,047
Eight: approval,

50
00:01:26,047 --> 00:01:26,810
promotion,

51
00:01:26,810 --> 00:01:27,496
rollback,

52
00:01:27,496 --> 00:01:28,869
and notifications.

53
00:01:28,869 --> 00:01:29,861
Nine: backup,

54
00:01:29,861 --> 00:01:30,471
upgrade,

55
00:01:30,471 --> 00:01:31,310
and triage.

56
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:34,932
Today one scenario uses the heart of all nine.

57
00:01:36,482 --> 00:01:41,282
The scenario. Release CloudCart, and prove it. Seven checks, run by a script.

58
00:01:41,832 --> 00:01:47,699
One: Jenkins answers, and your login works. Two: the job cloudcart-mastery exists.

59
00:01:48,249 --> 00:01:52,366
Three: the last build is a success. It ran Maven, and the tests.

60
00:01:52,916 --> 00:01:57,332
Four: the war file is archived. Five: a person approved the release.

61
00:01:57,882 --> 00:02:02,618
Six: the secret is masked in the log. Seven: a backup holds the job.

62
00:02:03,168 --> 00:02:07,307
The script checks the facts, not your word. That is what makes it independent.

63
00:02:07,857 --> 00:02:09,713
Seven of seven, is mastery.

64
00:02:11,263 --> 00:02:12,352
A real Jenkins,

65
00:02:12,352 --> 00:02:13,731
signed in as admin.

66
00:02:13,731 --> 00:02:14,601
It is empty.

67
00:02:14,601 --> 00:02:15,182
No jobs,

68
00:02:15,182 --> 00:02:17,069
and no release credential.

69
00:02:17,069 --> 00:02:18,666
We start from nothing.

70
00:02:20,016 --> 00:02:20,394
First,

71
00:02:20,394 --> 00:02:21,214
the terminal.

72
00:02:21,214 --> 00:02:23,044
The lab command is installed.

73
00:02:23,044 --> 00:02:25,253
Lab up checks that Jenkins answers,

74
00:02:25,253 --> 00:02:27,461
and says where the results will go.

75
00:02:28,011 --> 00:02:29,395
Now the check script.

76
00:02:29,395 --> 00:02:31,505
Lab check runs the seven checks.

77
00:02:31,505 --> 00:02:32,889
Nothing is built yet,

78
00:02:32,889 --> 00:02:34,142
so only one passes.

79
00:02:34,142 --> 00:02:36,779
Every failure tells you what to do next.

80
00:02:37,329 --> 00:02:38,816
Step one: the secret.

81
00:02:38,816 --> 00:02:40,728
Jenkins stores credentials,

82
00:02:40,728 --> 00:02:43,349
so a pipeline never holds a password.

83
00:02:43,349 --> 00:02:44,765
Open Manage Jenkins,

84
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:45,969
then Credentials.

85
00:02:49,019 --> 00:02:49,809
Then System,

86
00:02:49,809 --> 00:02:50,600
then Global.

87
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,893
These pages decide where a credential can be used.

88
00:02:53,893 --> 00:02:54,750
Global means,

89
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,528
everywhere in this Jenkins.

90
00:02:57,078 --> 00:03:01,174
And choose Add Credentials. Jenkins asks for the kind of credential.

91
00:03:01,724 --> 00:03:04,095
The kind is username with password.

92
00:03:04,095 --> 00:03:05,450
That is the default.

93
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:07,415
The username is dana-release.

94
00:03:07,415 --> 00:03:09,447
The password is a made up one.

95
00:03:09,447 --> 00:03:11,005
The ID is release-bot.

96
00:03:11,005 --> 00:03:13,647
That is the name the pipeline will use.

97
00:03:13,647 --> 00:03:14,460
Then Create.

98
00:03:18,410 --> 00:03:20,021
Step two: the pipeline.

99
00:03:20,021 --> 00:03:20,652
New Item,

100
00:03:20,652 --> 00:03:22,403
named cloudcart-mastery,

101
00:03:22,403 --> 00:03:23,594
of type Pipeline.

102
00:03:23,594 --> 00:03:26,255
This type runs a script that we write.

103
00:03:26,255 --> 00:03:26,816
Then OK.

104
00:03:30,966 --> 00:03:32,572
Read the script with me.

105
00:03:32,572 --> 00:03:33,376
Four stages.

106
00:03:33,376 --> 00:03:35,317
Build and test gets the code,

107
00:03:35,317 --> 00:03:36,857
and runs Maven package,

108
00:03:36,857 --> 00:03:38,598
which also runs the tests.

109
00:03:38,598 --> 00:03:40,406
Archive keeps the war file.

110
00:03:40,406 --> 00:03:42,213
Approve waits for a person.

111
00:03:42,213 --> 00:03:44,892
Release uses the credential release-bot,

112
00:03:44,892 --> 00:03:45,829
and prints it,

113
00:03:45,829 --> 00:03:47,904
to prove that Jenkins masks it.

114
00:03:48,454 --> 00:03:48,782
Save,

115
00:03:48,782 --> 00:03:49,698
and Build Now.

116
00:03:49,698 --> 00:03:51,335
Jenkins starts the build,

117
00:03:51,335 --> 00:03:52,710
and fetches the code.

118
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:54,150
Then open the console.

119
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:06,380
Maven builds,

120
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:07,666
and the tests pass.

121
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:09,832
The archive stage keeps the war.

122
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,388
Now the pipeline waits,

123
00:04:11,388 --> 00:04:12,810
at the Approve stage.

124
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:14,502
This is the release gate.

125
00:04:14,502 --> 00:04:16,329
Only a person can continue.

126
00:04:16,329 --> 00:04:17,276
Click Proceed.

127
00:04:20,326 --> 00:04:21,504
Finished: success.

128
00:04:21,504 --> 00:04:23,401
Now look at the release line.

129
00:04:23,401 --> 00:04:23,925
It says,

130
00:04:23,925 --> 00:04:25,626
releasing as dana-release,

131
00:04:25,626 --> 00:04:26,672
with four stars.

132
00:04:26,672 --> 00:04:28,177
The password is masked.

133
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:30,063
Back to the terminal.

134
00:04:30,063 --> 00:04:31,336
Run the check again.

135
00:04:31,336 --> 00:04:32,481
Six of seven pass.

136
00:04:32,481 --> 00:04:35,980
The one failure says exactly what is missing: a backup.

137
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:37,565
Make the backup.

138
00:04:37,565 --> 00:04:39,699
Lab backup archives Jenkins home.

139
00:04:39,699 --> 00:04:41,186
It takes a few seconds,

140
00:04:41,186 --> 00:04:42,738
and then shows the size.

141
00:04:43,288 --> 00:04:46,595
Check once more. Seven of seven. Every check passes.

142
00:04:53,745 --> 00:04:55,693
Results are part of the mastery.

143
00:04:55,693 --> 00:04:58,006
The check script saved them in a file.

144
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:58,554
Print it.

145
00:04:58,554 --> 00:05:00,442
This is your evidence: keep it,

146
00:05:00,442 --> 00:05:01,233
and share it.

147
00:05:01,783 --> 00:05:02,124
Last,

148
00:05:02,124 --> 00:05:02,942
the cleanup.

149
00:05:02,942 --> 00:05:05,261
Lab down deletes the scenario job,

150
00:05:05,261 --> 00:05:06,283
the credential,

151
00:05:06,283 --> 00:05:07,306
and the backup.

152
00:05:07,306 --> 00:05:09,079
Your Jenkins itself stays.

153
00:05:09,629 --> 00:05:11,488
Run the check one last time.

154
00:05:11,488 --> 00:05:13,347
Only the first check passes.

155
00:05:13,347 --> 00:05:14,476
Jenkins is alive,

156
00:05:14,476 --> 00:05:16,136
and the scenario is gone.

157
00:05:16,686 --> 00:05:17,632
In the browser,

158
00:05:17,632 --> 00:05:19,463
the dashboard is empty again.

159
00:05:19,463 --> 00:05:19,842
Built,

160
00:05:19,842 --> 00:05:20,284
proved,

161
00:05:20,284 --> 00:05:20,852
recorded,

162
00:05:20,852 --> 00:05:21,798
and cleaned up.

163
00:05:21,798 --> 00:05:22,808
That is mastery.

164
00:05:24,358 --> 00:05:27,025
When a check fails, the message tells you where to look.

165
00:05:27,575 --> 00:05:29,471
One: Jenkins does not answer.

166
00:05:29,471 --> 00:05:30,386
Is it running?

167
00:05:30,386 --> 00:05:31,564
Is the port right?

168
00:05:31,564 --> 00:05:33,591
Is the user and password right?

169
00:05:34,141 --> 00:05:37,789
Two: the job is missing. The name must match, letter for letter.

170
00:05:38,339 --> 00:05:42,328
Three: the build is red. Open the console, and read the first error.

171
00:05:42,878 --> 00:05:46,355
Four: no artifact. Check the archive step, and its path.

172
00:05:46,905 --> 00:05:50,916
Five: no approval. The input step must be answered by a person.

173
00:05:51,466 --> 00:05:56,394
Six: the secret is visible. Never echo plain text. Use with credentials.

174
00:05:56,944 --> 00:06:00,123
Seven: no backup. Run lab backup, and check again.

175
00:06:01,673 --> 00:06:04,468
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

176
00:06:05,018 --> 00:06:06,482
One: the repository,

177
00:06:06,482 --> 00:06:10,802
github.com/it-waves/devops-ai,

178
00:06:10,802 --> 00:06:13,146
in the folder academy/lab.

179
00:06:13,696 --> 00:06:19,712
Two: the files, lab163.sh, and shortcuts163.sh.

180
00:06:20,262 --> 00:06:25,723
Three: install it, with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin.

181
00:06:26,273 --> 00:06:31,798
Four: load the short names, with source shortcuts163.sh. Then lab up.

182
00:06:32,348 --> 00:06:38,194
Five: lab check runs the seven checks. Lab backup makes the archive. Lab down cleans up.

183
00:06:38,744 --> 00:06:42,221
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson 155,

184
00:06:42,221 --> 00:06:42,811
and Java.

185
00:06:42,811 --> 00:06:45,698
Set your login in the variable JENKINS_AUTH.

186
00:06:46,248 --> 00:06:47,891
The link is in the description.

187
00:06:49,441 --> 00:06:51,212
Your turn, on your own machine.

188
00:06:51,762 --> 00:06:54,812
One: lab up, then lab check. See the failures first.

189
00:06:55,362 --> 00:06:59,629
Two: add the credential release-bot. Then create the pipeline, and build it.

190
00:07:00,179 --> 00:07:02,995
Three: approve the release, and read the masked line.

191
00:07:03,545 --> 00:07:07,364
Four: lab backup, and lab check, until you see seven of seven.

192
00:07:07,914 --> 00:07:11,604
Five: keep the results file as your evidence. Then lab down.

193
00:07:12,154 --> 00:07:13,989
Pause the video, and begin now.

194
00:07:29,539 --> 00:07:30,414
Quick check.

195
00:07:30,964 --> 00:07:32,841
Which check proves a secret is safe?

196
00:07:33,391 --> 00:07:36,015
Why does a release need a person to approve it?

197
00:07:36,565 --> 00:07:38,229
What makes this check independent?

198
00:07:38,779 --> 00:07:40,422
What did you clean up, and why?

199
00:07:40,972 --> 00:07:46,454
Objective covered: MC17, the mastery evidence. The whole Jenkins domain.

200
00:07:47,004 --> 00:07:49,074
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

201
00:07:59,624 --> 00:08:04,125
Next: a new domain. SonarQube, and how it keeps code quality honest.

202
00:08:04,675 --> 00:08:08,003
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
